WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.408
[MUSIC]

00:00:10.408 --> 00:00:15.748
Why would the banks disrupt themselves by
introducing a digital currency that would

00:00:15.748 --> 00:00:20.724
make it easier for consumers and
businesses to dis-intermediate the banks?

00:00:20.724 --> 00:00:24.890
Well, the banks may not be the innovators.

00:00:24.890 --> 00:00:30.215
It may be that they are the reactors,
that they will react when others innovate.

00:00:30.215 --> 00:00:35.120
And I'm sure that they've consider
the trade offs involved in whether

00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:40.720
to disrupt themselves by
introducing digital currencies,

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:44.710
or whether to wait and react when
others introduce digital currencies.

00:00:44.710 --> 00:00:47.310
Right now digital currency
sounds very edgy and

00:00:47.310 --> 00:00:51.790
kind of alternative lifestyle,
but it's becoming the mainstream.

00:00:51.790 --> 00:00:55.510
And so, the largest banks in
particular are very aware of this,

00:00:55.510 --> 00:00:59.000
they're investing in the technology,
and they will provide this service

00:01:00.140 --> 00:01:05.510
as soon as it's profitable enough,
after considering the cost

00:01:05.510 --> 00:01:09.570
to them of losing some of their current
business that they're going to disrupt.

00:01:09.570 --> 00:01:15.644
Banks will eventually either be leading,
or following, but they'll be involved.

00:01:15.644 --> 00:01:16.527
They can't avoid it.

00:01:16.527 --> 00:01:25.818
[MUSIC]

